2026-09-19 00:55:24,391 - --- Processing Patient Record 101 ---
2026-09-19 00:55:24,391 - Phase 1 (Input): Loaded raw continuous ECG signal. Shape: (650000, 2). Represents ~30 mins of 2-lead recordings at 360Hz.
2026-09-19 00:55:24,408 - Phase 2 (Filtering): Applied 0.5-45Hz Butterworth filter. Effect: Baseline wander (patient breathing drift) and electrical noise eliminated. The signal's isoelectric baseline is now completely flat.
2026-09-19 00:55:24,414 - Phase 3 (Extraction): Segmented 1859 valid beats using R-peaks. Effect: Morphed continuous signal into discrete 198-sample windows. Combined Lead 1 and Lead 2 into a 396-dimensional morphological vector.
2026-09-19 00:55:24,470 - Phase 4 (Normalization): Applied independent Z-score normalization per lead. Effect: Scaled varying peak amplitudes down to a standard range. The model will now learn the physical *shape* of the heartbeat rather than its raw voltage size.
2026-09-19 00:55:24,470 - Phase 5 (Routing): Patient assigned to TRAIN set (DS1).
